{
  "$comment": [
    "Single source of truth for AlloyFlux's externally-controllable parameters.",
    "",
    "Generated consumers (run `make params` after editing, and commit the output",
    "so a normal build never needs Python):",
    "  include/param_manifest.generated.h  — C++ descriptor table",
    "  ../../web-configurator/src/lib/paramMap.generated.ts  (slice 3)",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  cc        MIDI CC number, also the identity used by SysEx patch dumps",
    "  name      serial command name and web key — must stay stable, it is API",
    "  label     human label for the web UI",
    "  category  web UI grouping; order comes from `categories` below",
    "  kind      float | enum | bool",
    "  min/max   float only. `symbol` allows a C++ constant (e.g. DELAY_MAX_MS)",
    "  scale     float only: linear | log",
    "  target    C++ lvalue the dispatcher writes; must match `kind`",
    "  options   enum only: labels in CC-band order, low to high",
    "",
    "Params NOT listed here are genuinely not parameters — CC 64 sustain,",
    "CC 119 drone return and CC 123 panic are actions, and stay hand-written in",
    "usb_midi.cpp. CC 16 (root pitch) is also special: it carries a V/Oct",
    "encoding rather than a plain range."
  ],
  "$comment_includes": "Headers the generated C++ table needs for its `target` lvalues and any `symbol` bounds.",
  "ts_output": "../../web-configurator/src/lib/paramMapAlloyFlux.ts",
  "cpp_includes": [
    "params.h",
    "dsp/ReverbEngine.h",
    "dsp/DelayEngine.h",
    "dsp/FxChain.h"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Voice",
    "Oscillator",
    "Animation",
    "Envelope",
    "Filter",
    "FX Chain",
    "Output",
    "Chorus",
    "Reverb",
    "Delay"
  ],
