      "min": 27.5,
      "max": 7040.0,
      "default": 440.0,
      "scale": "log",
      "unit": "Hz",
      "target": "gBaseFreq",
      "$comment": "Was hand-coded as a ±4 V/Oct offset: freq = 440·2^(−4 + 8t). That is identical to a log sweep from 440·2⁻⁴ = 27.5 Hz to 440·2⁴ = 7040 Hz, so it needs no special case.",
      "$comment_display": "27.5–7040 Hz is exactly 8 octaves centred on 440 Hz, so the same sweep reads as −48…+48 semitones with 0 at centre — the Plaits convention. Firmware still stores Hz; only the UI changes units, and the CC sent is identical either way.",
      "display": {
        "min": -48,
        "max": 48,
        "unit": "st",
        "scale": "linear"
